lsy|n|The state of being difficult, or hard to do; hardness; arduousness; -- opposed to easiness or facility; as, the difficulty of a task or enterprise; a work of difficulty. ; Something difficult; a thing hard to do or to understand; that which occasions labor or perplexity, and requires skill and perseverance to overcome, solve, or achieve; a hard enterprise; an obstacle; an impediment; as, the difficulties of a science; difficulties in theology. ; A controversy; a falling out; a disagreement; an objection; a cavil. ; Embarrassment of affairs, especially financial affairs; -- usually in the plural; as, to be in difficulties.	a:qok,56,4;ynh,48,12;150m,47,3;oq7,45,5;ff9,44,5;yne,41,51;1uxf,39,8;rbm,37,8;t23,34,5;8b1,34,3;1zxr,27,8;1bgw,27,19;1ttl,27,19;13d,25,12;27vu,22,7~22gw,6,56;yne,41,51;1fiq,17,44;1f74,4,41;1bgw,27,19;1ttl,27,19;1abn,18,14;ynh,48,12;13d,25,12;212m,10,11;4il,19,8;rbm,37,8;1zxr,27,8;1uxf,39,8;10xe,18,8	v:t81,54,12;143d,52,10;1mhm,38,5;2eac,37,2;t76,24,5;27pl,20,6;c9p,14,4;ubd,14,4;12w,7,3;1xvf,6,22;ub8,3,16~1xvf,6,22;ub8,3,16;t81,54,12;143d,52,10;27pl,20,6;1mhm,38,5;t76,24,5;ubd,14,4;c9p,14,4;12w,7,3;2eac,37,2	V:1tyv,94,10;1uru,79,2;1agf,77,5;1u8c,74,17;5vl,71,8;fpl,70,4;nb1,68,6;4x4,67,9;1zau,66,7;12x0,66,5;1v2m,63,6;fds,58,12;ubd,58,81;161d,56,5;19vh,55,9~xgz,41,91;ubd,58,81;2ci7,46,55;1u8c,74,17;1bj4,20,14;1qwv,29,13;1tst,20,12;fds,58,12;v5n,16,11;1tyv,94,10;np0,3,10;19vh,55,9;4x4,67,9;5vl,71,8;1zau,66,7	n:t23,34,5;13f5,25,3;s8l,13,6;17yd,11,4;hoa,5,13;t76,1,1~hoa,5,13;s8l,13,6;t23,34,5;17yd,11,4;13f5,25,3;t76,1,1	N:18m,51,3;4x4,45,2;19ov,44,9;19om,43,70;19vh,34,2;1r1m,28,4;2e9e,27,3;1ysz,23,5;io,21,2;1yd0,17,2;2ci7,14,6;f7f,8,4~19om,43,70;19ov,44,9;2ci7,14,6;1ysz,23,5;f7f,8,4;1r1m,28,4;18m,51,3;2e9e,27,3;19vh,34,2;1yd0,17,2;io,21,2;4x4,45,2
